      "refersTo": "chip-shift-long",
      "description": "Shifts are filled with their hue; leave is outlined with its state; a gap is a red outline.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-chip ds-long\">Long day</span> <span class=\"ds-chip ds-night\">Night</span> <span class=\"ds-chip ds-off\">RDO</span> <span class=\"ds-chip ds-leave ds-wait\">Annual</span> <span class=\"ds-chip ds-leave ds-ok\">Annual</span> <span class=\"ds-chip ds-leave ds-no\">Annual</span> <span class=\"ds-needs\">Needs night</span>",
      "css": ":host{--re-ink:#1f2933;--re-muted:#5c6670;--re-line:#dfe3e8;--re-line-strong:#aab3bc;--re-panel:#f6f7f9;--re-accent:#0b5ed7;--re-bad:#b42318;--re-bad-bg:#fdf0ee;--re-bad-line:#e4a1a8;--re-ok:#146c43;--re-ok-bg:#edf7f1;--re-ok-line:#9fd3b5;--re-wait:#7a4a00;--re-wait-bg:#fff4d6;--re-wait-line:#d9a63a;--re-long:#b54708;--re-night:#1d2b5c;--re-off-bg:#eef0f3;--re-off-ink:#3d4650;--re-off-line:#8a949e;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;color:var(--re-ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-chip{display:inline-block;padding:3px 4px;border:1px solid transparent;border-radius:4px;font:500 .75rem/1 inherit;white-space:nowrap}.ds-long{background:var(--re-long);color:#fff}.ds-night{background:var(--re-night);color:#fff}.ds-off{border:1px dashed var(--re-off-line);background:var(--re-off-bg);color:var(--re-off-ink)}.ds-leave{padding-inline:3px}.ds-wait{border-color:var(--re-wait-line);background:var(--re-wait-bg);color:var(--re-wait)}.ds-ok{border-color:var(--re-ok-line);background:var(--re-ok-bg);color:var(--re-ok)}.ds-no{border-color:var(--re-bad-line);background:#fff;color:var(--re-bad);text-decoration:line-through}.ds-needs{display:inline-block;padding:1px 5px;border:1px solid var(--re-bad);border-radius:3px;background:#fff;color:var(--re-bad);font:600 .6875rem/1.3 inherit;cursor:pointer}.ds-needs:hover{background:var(--re-bad-bg)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Clause Tag",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "clause-tag",
      "description": "The contract clause beside a rule break.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-clause\">STONZ 17.1.2</span> More than 72 hours in 7 days",
      "css": ":host{--re-ink:#1f2933;--re-muted:#5c6670;--re-line:#dfe3e8;--re-line-strong:#aab3bc;--re-panel:#f6f7f9;--re-accent:#0b5ed7;--re-bad:#b42318;--re-bad-bg:#fdf0ee;--re-bad-line:#e4a1a8;--re-ok:#146c43;--re-ok-bg:#edf7f1;--re-ok-line:#9fd3b5;--re-wait:#7a4a00;--re-wait-bg:#fff4d6;--re-wait-line:#d9a63a;--re-long:#b54708;--re-night:#1d2b5c;--re-off-bg:#eef0f3;--re-off-ink:#3d4650;--re-off-line:#8a949e;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;color:var(--re-ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-clause{display:inline-block;margin-right:.375rem;padding:0 4px;border:1px solid var(--re-bad-line);border-radius:3px;color:var(--re-bad);font:600 .6875rem/1.5 inherit}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tabs",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tab",
      "description": "A panel-grey well of tabs; the selected tab lifts to white.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tabs\"><button class=\"ds-tab is-on\">Waiting on you <span class=\"ds-count\">2</span></button><button class=\"ds-tab\">All waiting <span class=\"ds-count\">5</span></button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Decided lately</button></div>",
      "css": ":host{--re-ink:#1f2933;--re-muted:#5c6670;--re-line:#dfe3e8;--re-line-strong:#aab3bc;--re-panel:#f6f7f9;--re-accent:#0b5ed7;--re-bad:#b42318;--re-bad-bg:#fdf0ee;--re-bad-line:#e4a1a8;--re-ok:#146c43;--re-ok-bg:#edf7f1;--re-ok-line:#9fd3b5;--re-wait:#7a4a00;--re-wait-bg:#fff4d6;--re-wait-line:#d9a63a;--re-long:#b54708;--re-night:#1d2b5c;--re-off-bg:#eef0f3;--re-off-ink:#3d4650;--re-off-line:#8a949e;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;color:var(--re-ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-tabs{display:inline-flex;gap:2px;padding:3px;border:1px solid var(--re-line);border-radius:.5rem;background:var(--re-panel)}.ds-tab{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.375rem;padding:.3125rem .75rem;border:0;border-radius:.375rem;background:transparent;color:var(--re-muted);font:500 .875rem/1.5 inherit;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 120ms ease-out,color 120ms ease-out}.ds-tab:hover{color:var(--re-ink)}.ds-tab:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--re-accent);outline-offset:1px}.ds-tab.is-on{background:#fff;color:var(--re-ink);box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(31,41,51,.12)}.ds-count{min-width:1.25rem;padding:0 .375rem;border-radius:999px;background:var(--re-line);color:var(--re-off-ink);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:600;text-align:center}.is-on .ds-count{background:#e8f0fe;color:#0a4bab}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Navbar",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "navbar",
      "description": "The dark global bar with the amber mark: the registrar's pages, the admin group behind a rule with a waiting count, and how far the roster is published; the current page is underlined in amber.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\"><span class=\"ds-brand\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"#ffc107\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 .5a.5.5 0 0 0-1 0V1H2a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v11a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V3a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-1V.5a.5.5 0 0 0-1 0V1H4zM1 14V4h14v10a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H2a1 1 0 0 1-1-1m7-6.507c1.664-1.711 5.825 1.283 0 5.132-5.825-3.85-1.664-6.843 0-5.132\"/></svg>Radscheduler</span><a class=\"ds-link\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Calendar</a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">My leave</a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Extra duties</a><span class=\"ds-sep\"></span><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Roster editor</a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Leave requests<span class=\"ds-pill\">3</span></a><span class=\"ds-status\">Roster published to <b>Tue 2 Feb</b></span></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.25rem;padding:.25rem .75rem;background:#212529;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:.875rem}.ds-brand{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-right:1rem;color:#fff;font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:600}.ds-link{padding:.5rem .625rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.68);font-weight:500;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap}.ds-link:hover{color:rgba(255,255,255,.9)}.ds-link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #ffc107;outline-offset:2px;border-radius:.375rem}.ds-link[aria-current=page]{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline 2px #ffc107;text-underline-offset:.45em}.ds-sep{align-self:stretch;margin:0 .5rem;border-left:1px solid #6c757d}.ds-pill{display:inline-block;min-width:1.25rem;margin-left:.375rem;padding:0 .375rem;border-radius:999px;background:#ffc107;color:#1f2933;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25rem;text-align:center}.ds-status{margin-left:auto;color:rgba(255,255,255,.68);font-size:.8125rem;white-space:nowrap}.ds-status b{color:#fff;font-weight:500}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Undo Toast",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "toast",
      "description": "A charcoal toast that carries undo for a few seconds after a decision.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-toast\"><span>Approved 2 days of Erika Lee's annual leave.</span><button class=\"ds-ondark\">Undo</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-toast{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.75rem;max-width:36rem;padding:.5rem .625rem .5rem .875rem;border-radius:.5rem;background:#2b2f33;color:#fff;font:.875rem/1.4 system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(15,23,42,.25)}.ds-ondark{min-height:2rem;padding:.25rem .625rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.35);border-radius:.375rem;background:transparent;color:#fff;font:500 .875rem/1.25 inherit;cursor:pointer}.ds-ondark:hover{border-color:#fff;background:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}.ds-ondark:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #9ec5fe;outline-offset:1px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Duty Board",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Duty Board\"**\n\nRadscheduler is the department's whiteboard made trustworthy. The board's job is to be read at a glance by someone between cases, and to be rewritten all day by the senior registrar. Every mark on it means something: a filled chip is a shift, an outlined chip is leave, a red outline is a gap or a rule break with its clause beside it. Nothing on the board is decoration, and nothing that matters relies on colour alone.\n\nIt is dense but friendly. The roster editor packs three weeks of registrars onto one wide screen, so type is small (13–14px body, 11–12px chips) and controls share one compact size. Long editing sessions shouldn't feel harsh, though, so corners stay softly rounded, lines are hairline greys rather than black rules, hover feedback is a quiet tint, and popovers rise gently over 120ms. Registrars use the same pages on a phone, where the same chips and states read at full width.\n\nThe system lives in the Elm pages (`static/css/editor_elm.scss` and `leave_requests.scss`, all `--re-*` tokens). The older Bootstrap templates (calendar, leave, extra duties, admin-adjacent pages) are legacy and should move toward these tokens rather than the other way round. The app rejects the generic SaaS dashboard (card grids, big KPI numbers, gradients, soft shadows on everything) and hospital IT (grey enterprise forms, tiny controls, cramped dialogs, a colour soup of status codes).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One light, neutral working surface; colour is reserved for shifts and for three states (ok, waiting, bad).",
      "Shapes and line styles carry meaning as well as colour: fill, outline, dash, strike-through, folded corner.",
      "One compact control size (2rem) everywhere; tabular numerals throughout.",
      "Flat at rest; only floating layers cast a shadow.",
      "The dark navbar and its amber mark frame every page; amber appears nowhere else."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three States Rule",
        "body": "Decisions and checks have exactly three colours: green for approved or covered, ochre for waiting, red for declined, gaps and breaches. A new status takes one of these with a distinct shape or icon. Never add a fourth state colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Amber Is the Mark Rule",
        "body": "Amber belongs to the logo and the dark navbar. On light surfaces the accent is Roster Blue, always.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Contrast Floor Rule",
        "body": "Every text pair meets WCAG AA, and every mark that carries meaning on its own (markers, edges, outlines) meets 3:1 against its ground. Check any new pair before shipping it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every Elm surface sets `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`. Dates, hours and loads must line up in columns.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Full Name Rule",
        "body": "A chip keeps its full label where it can (busy days stack chips one per line and the row grows); when space truly runs out, it ends in an ellipsis rather than wrapping.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wide Screen, Short Burst Rule",
        "body": "Design the editor for a wide desktop and long sessions; design registrar pages for a phone and a glance. The same tokens serve both; density changes, meaning doesn't.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Floating Only Rule",
        "body": "A shadow means \"this is above the board and will go away\". Resting surfaces, chips, cells and buttons never cast one.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do give every state a cue beyond colour: an icon, a dash, a strike-through, a fold, an underline or a word.",
      "Do fill shifts and outline everything else: leave, gaps, clause tags and badges.",
      "Do use the `--re-*` tokens on any new page, and bring legacy Bootstrap pages toward them when you touch them.",
      "Do keep controls at the one 2rem size, with a 2px Roster Blue focus outline (amber on the dark navbar).",
      "Do mark unpublished, pending or stale data explicitly, with the unpublished hatch or a tag, never by omission.",
      "Do keep motion to colour transitions and the 120ms popover rise, and turn it off under `prefers-reduced-motion`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't build card grids, hero metrics, gradients or soft shadows on resting surfaces; this is not a SaaS dashboard.",
      "Don't shrink controls below 2rem, cram dialogs, or add status colours beyond the three states; this is not hospital IT.",
      "Don't use amber anywhere but the logo and the navbar.",
      "Don't use Bootstrap's default blue (#0d6efd) or its glow focus shadow on Elm pages.",
      "Don't fill a gap or a leave chip with a hue, or it will read as a shift.",
      "Don't add a second typeface or a display face."
    ]
  }
}
